fix(worker): refresh all quota windows from unifiedWindows (#4068)

RateLimitStore keys each rate_limit_event by its binding rateLimitType, almost
always five_hour, so a seven_day reading is only written by the rare event
bound to seven_day. A stale high seven_day reading (e.g. from before an account
switch) then trips shouldAbortForQuota for the life of the worker. set() now
fans rate_limit_info.unifiedWindows out to the per-window buckets and backfills
the binding window's utilization from it.

Rebased 2026-10-01 onto upstream v13.28.0, which already ignores expired
snapshots and normalizes epoch-seconds resetsAt (the rest of the original
#4072 cherry-pick), so only the fan-out remains.
